==Upgrades==
The avernic treads can be upgraded by using a pair of [[Primordial boots|primordial]], [[Eternal boots|eternal]], and [[pegasian boots]] on it. These boots may be added in any order, and it's entirely possible to only add one or two pair of boots to these treads.

Players must have 80 [[Magic]] and 60 [[Runecraft]] to add any upgrade, in addition to 4,000 [[demon tear]]s per pair of boots (12,000 demon tears in total). As soon as at least one upgrade has been added, the treads become ''untradeable''. This process is reversible, returning the base avernic treads and all pairs of boots used on it - however, any spent demon tears will be lost.

Upgrading the treads only affects the bonuses of the associated combat style, e.g. adding [[primordial boots]] will increase the treads' melee strength bonus:

* {{plink|Primordial boots}}: +2 melee strength
* {{plink|Pegasian boots}}: +1 ranged strength
* {{plink|Eternal boots}}: +1% magic damage

Once fully upgraded, the boots become [[avernic treads (max)]]. In addition to the cost of the avernic treads themselves, the [[Grand Exchange]] cost of fully upgrading the treads is {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Demon tear|12000}} + {{GEP|Primordial boots}} + {{GEP|Eternal boots}} + {{GEP|Pegasian boots}}|c}}, giving a total cost of {{NoCoins|{{GEP|Demon tear|12000}} + {{GEP|Primordial boots}} + {{GEP|Eternal boots}} + {{GEP|Pegasian boots}} + {{GEP|Avernic treads}}|c}}.

{{Avernic treads table}}

If the boots are lost on [[PvP]] death, the base avernic treads and any applied boots will be dropped for the killer and all used tears will be lost.

Any upgraded version of the avernic treads may be used as a replacement for the [[dragon boots]] in the elite [[STASH]] hole near the [[Fountain of Heroes]] inside the [[Heroes' Guild]]. The base treads cannot be stored there.

