==Development==
The treads were originally required to have all three boot sets (primordial, pegasian, and eternal), which would be combined with an [[avernic catalyst]]. The boots would have had three different recolour options.{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/varlamore-the-final-dawn-quest-delve-boss--slayer-dungeon-rewards?oldschool=1|title=Varlamore: The Final Dawn Quest, Delve Boss & Slayer Dungeon Rewards|newsdate=9 January 2025|quote=The Avernic Catalyst is a consumable item that can be used together with the Primordial, Pegasian ''and'' Eternal boots (you'll need all three) to create the Avernic Treads. This conversion is irreversible but would include three recolours to make sure your new shoes fit your FashionScape.}} Player concerns quickly arose about the requirement of pegasian boots, as [[ranger boots]] were much harder to acquire compared to [[dragon boots]] and [[infinity boots]], respectively. The new requirements were revealed on [[11 March]] [[2025]], accounting for player feedback about the treads. Due to the new requirements allowing players to add one boot at a time, the three different recolours were scrapped due to it complicating the work that would have to be done, and was replaced with all upgraded versions of the boots appearing identical to one another.{{CiteNews|url=https://secure.runescape.com/m=news/new-delve-boss-rewards---varlamore-the-final-dawn?oldschool=1|title=New Delve Boss Rewards - Varlamore: The Final Dawn|newsdate=11 March 2025|quote=While we wanted to offer three different aesthetic options for these boots, the new design proposal complicates the work required to do that, so we will be proceeding with just one, still very stylish, option:}}

